It needs a power press: hold Power ~10-15 s, release, press Power normally.
Do NOT power-cycle before considering this: the payload's log lives in the top of
DRAM and is lost on a cold boot, so a power cycle also loses whatever the run
produced. If the payload armed its watchdog, the reboot that returns the device
would have preserved the log - so a failure to return means the log is likely
unrecoverable anyway, but waiting is free and power-cycling is not.

BUT: a non-returning run's log may still be recoverable. What destroys it is a cold power
transition or a NEW `fastboot boot` (any later kernel clears the buffer on entry) - not every
reset. Boot the STOCK ANDROID image directly (its kernel is what reads the console):
  VolDown+Power -> fastboot -> `fastboot boot /mnt/data/mi4-ios6/xiaomi4-cancro-backup-20260604-112053/boot.img` -> in the Android shell,
  `cat /proc/last_kmsg`   # returns the *previous* boot's RAM console
Do NOT boot TWRP first: its kernel has no `/proc/last_kmsg` AND its boot takes the slot
the log is in. The watchdog sentence above is the case where recovery fails outright.
